# THE HOLDING'S DAILY COPY — systemd USER unit (install: scripts/systemd/install.sh).
#
# WHY IT EXISTS, and it is a repair, not a new idea. The company's database was
# dumped nightly and shipped to the Hetzner Storage Box from 2026-07-18. The
# move to the workstation (board row B29) carried the repository, the database,
# the keys and the toolchain — and left the SCHEDULE behind on the X230: the
# script's own header still installs a cron line under /home/ghost. Measured
# 2026-08-27: no crontab for this user, no dxb timer of any kind, and the last
# automatic dump was 2026-08-13. Thirteen days in which the holding existed on
# one desk and nowhere else.
#
# It writes the night's set — a custom-format pg_dump of the COMPANY engine
# (supabase_db_DxB_Global_OS), its roles and a manifest — to ~/backups/dxb,
# copies tonight's dump to the off-site destination, reading it back before
# calling it landed, and prunes the sets older than 14 days only on a night
# proven on both sides. It opens no other door and carries no credential of its
# own. Installed, with its timer and its alert, by scripts/backup/install-units.sh.
#
# B72, 2026-11-22. The Storage Box is gone, so the destination is a SETTING and
# no longer an address in the script: BACKUP_DEST in ~/.config/dxb/backup.env
# (the leading "-" lets the file be absent). While it is unset the job fails
# every night, on purpose — a night without an off-site copy is a failed night
# — and OnFailure= says so on the desktop (dxb-backup-alert.service).
#
# It logs to the JOURNAL, so nothing has to be opened before the script starts;
# the script appends its own lines to ~/backups/dxb/backup.log once that folder
# is there. A oneshot has no start timeout unless it is given one: a hung
# docker or transfer is cut off after 30 minutes, which fails the unit and
# raises the alert like any other failure.
[Unit]
Description=DXB — daily dump of the holding's database, with the off-site copy
OnFailure=dxb-backup-alert.service

[Service]
Type=oneshot
EnvironmentFile=-%h/.config/dxb/backup.env
ExecStart=/usr/bin/bash "%h/DxB Global OS/scripts/backup/laptop-pg-dump.sh"
TimeoutStartSec=30min
